      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The sequence of events is clear: a late-season coaching change saw John Tortorella, the turnaround specialist, installed with eight regular-season games remaining. His immediate tactical improvement was evident, guiding the team to a 7-0-1 record, followed by sequential playoff progression past Utah and Anaheim. This foundation allowed the team to advance, with their championship series qualification secured after a decisive series conclusion. The cause-and-effect is verified: strategic managerial intervention at a critical juncture directly enabled this postseason advancement.",
