    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "A significant factor in the outcome was the injury-caused absence of Colorado's key personnel, namely the athletes Cale Makar and Nathan MacKinnon. This key personnel depletion fundamentally altered the competitive dynamic. Against this backdrop, the dominant victors from Vegas demonstrated defensive mastery in the playoff series, holding the injury-plagued contenders to a single goal in the final game. The verified chronology shows how the winning team's execution, built on a strong coaching performance, led to their finals berth.",
